st does less damage and  his agitated mode his body is rock-hard  and most of your attacks will bounce off  of him there are other differences but  we will get into those differences in a  second I just wanted to let you guys  know that ahead of time and also when  you're hit by Kieran's moves there is a  chance you're going to contract a  thunder blight this needs to be removed  immediately because this could cause  either paralysis leaving you open to  another attack or causes lots of damage  to you simply eating those low berries  we talked about earlier will get rid of  the effects so make sure to stockpile  some before the fight for his moveset  like I said before it's mostly all going  to be Thunder attacks one move he does  is this a wee thunder move where he  shoots lightning around him they will  land in the same five spots every single  time  for near his top leg and back legs and  one at the top near his horn just like  in the clip shown the agitated version  of this though is that instead of  sending five it's going to be ten  lightning strikes the other five are  going to be Indy five other places that  the original five lightning strikes  weren't the Lightning will basically  surround him leaving you unable to  attack him it's better to wait until all  the lightning is done striking to attack  and then another move is this bigger  lightning strike work here in black  lightning in front of him except it's  bigger and has a bigger area and does  more damage  once again simply running out of the way  of it dodging all that good stuff and  you will completely negate all the  damage for it next move is the lines of  lightning Kieran will summon these few  lines of lightning stay out of the path  there it will basically have a blue line  on the floor if you stand in between  them you'll be perfectly safe you just  have to be in that perfect safe zone if  you want to you can also if you want to  be risky you can use this opportunity to  charge Kieran since it